<BaseLayout title="About Jonathan — THIEPN" description="The person behind THIEPN: Jonathan, making browser tools, games, learning systems and longer-form work.">
<article class="page-shell page-content about-studio"><header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The person behind the projects</p><h1>I’m Jonathan.<br/>This is my workshop.</h1><p class="about-lead">THIEPN is where I share the things I make: software you can use, games you can play, and ideas you can spend time with.</p></header>
<section class="story-section"><h2>Mathematics, languages<br/>and making things.</h2><div class="prose"><p>I study Wirtschaftsmathematik in Cologne. Mathematics, languages and faith run through the work here: tools that make a task easier, systems for practice, and longer-form writing about discipleship and mission.</p><p>Games are another part of the workshop. Sometimes the result is a small mechanic worth playing; sometimes it becomes a larger application. The projects are different, but each needs a clear first action and a reason to come back.</p></div></section>
<section class="story-section"><h2>How the work gets made.</h2><div class="prose"><p>A project is more than its first working version. I keep working on the interface, the core experience and the implementation. The repositories show the code and revision history behind the work.</p><p>Where possible, I favor browser-based, local-first tools: fewer barriers between opening a project and trying it. Not every project is finished. Beta and experimental work is labelled, and the archive keeps earlier work accessible without treating it all as equally representative.</p></div></section>
<section class="story-section"><h2>A closer look.</h2><div class="evidence-links"><a href="/project/tiny-tools/"><strong>Tiny Tools</strong><span>Focused tasks, shared engines and explicit limits →</span></a><a href="/project/micro-arcade/"><strong>Micro Arcade</strong><span>A shared shell for many small games →</span></a><a href="/project/pdf-studio/"><strong>PDF Studio</strong><span>A practical document workspace →</span></a><a href="/project/manuscript/"><strong>Manuscript</strong><span>From structured writing to publication →</span></a><a href="/library/"><strong>The Library</strong><span>Longer-form work, made for reading →</span></a></div></section>
